  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What happens to total resistance when resistors are added in parallel?', 'It decreases, and is less than the smallest individual resistance.', 14),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'How is an ammeter connected?', 'In series with the component.', 15),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'How is a voltmeter connected?', 'In parallel across the component.', 16),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the I–V graph for a fixed resistor?', 'A straight line through the origin.', 17),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the I–V graph for a filament lamp?', 'A curve that gets less steep, because resistance increases as the filament heats up.', 18),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the I–V graph for a diode?', 'Current flows in one direction only, after a small threshold voltage.', 19),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'How does the resistance of a thermistor change?', 'It decreases as temperature increases.', 20),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'How does the resistance of an LDR change?', 'It decreases as light intensity increases.', 21),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is electrical power?', 'P = IV = I²R.', 22),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'Calculate the power of a lamp with 230 V and 0.5 A.', 'P = 230 × 0.5 = 115 W.', 23),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the equation for energy transferred electrically?', 'E = IVt (or E = QV).', 24),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the difference between AC and DC?', 'AC changes direction regularly; DC flows in one direction only.', 25),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the UK mains supply?', 'AC at 230 V and 50 Hz.', 26),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What are the three wires in a UK plug?', 'Live (brown), neutral (blue) and earth (green and yellow).', 27),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the purpose of the earth wire?', 'It stops the casing becoming live, preventing electric shocks if there is a fault.', 28),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'What is the purpose of a fuse?', 'It melts and breaks the circuit if the current is too high, protecting the appliance and preventing fires.', 29),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.2', 'Electricity', 'Why does a current in a resistor cause heating?', 'Electrons collide with ions in the lattice, transferring energy and making them vibrate more.', 30),
  ('Physics', 'AQA', 'gcse', '4.3', 'Particle Model of Matter', 'What is density?', 'Mass per unit volume: ρ = m/V.', 1),
